   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to providing for the\nfinancing and construction of facilities by the dormitory authority for North\nCountry School",
    "basePrintNo": "S8059",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8059-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8059\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to providing for the financing and construction of facilities\nby the dormitory authority for North Country School\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides for the financing and construction of facilities by\nthe Dormitory Authority for the State of New York (DASNY) for the North\nCountry School in Lake Placid.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1 amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 2 of section 1676 of the\npublic authorities law by adding a new undesignated paragraph.\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision 1 of section 1680 of the public authorities\nlaw by adding a new undesignated paragraph.\n\nSection 3 qualifies North Country School contracts as state contracts.\n\nSection 4 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe North Country School, located in Lake Placid, is a non-profit\nboarding/day school for students in grades 4-9th established in 1938,\nand is currently a member of the NYSAIS (New York State Association of\nIndependent Schools). This bill would extend DASNY financing and\nconstruction authorization to the North Country School under the Dormi-\ntory Authority Act as an educational institution to allow bonding for\nupcoming capital projects.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
